  * patch 0074.
  *
  * Every path carries the participating objects it is inside, in order of entry, with the IOR read
- * at entry (shadow paths: objects only). A participating hit on object X is "masked" (a buried
+ * at entry (shadow paths: objects only). A negative stored IOR marks wavelength dependence;
+ * its magnitude is the positive absolute IOR at the shared path wavelength. The sign is retained
+ * verbatim by camera/SSS probes and CPU/GPU stack copies, and decoded only at a real interface. A participating hit on object X is "masked" (a buried
  * boundary the ray passes straight through) when another entry has a higher priority. Otherwise
  * the closures use the relative IOR against the "opposite" medium: the highest entry below X
  * (ties: entered first), or air. See artifacts/feature-nested/DESIGN.md.
